<title>UK: Russia's GAZ auto firm gets EBRD loan.</title>
<headline>Russia's GAZ auto firm gets EBRD loan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) said on Friday it would lend $65 million to Russian vehicle manufacturer GAZ.</p>
<p>The money will finance the purchase and installation of new facilities for the Volga passenger car, the only medium-sized family saloon car produced in Russia, the Bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It is the second loan by the EBRD to the company, after a $25 million loan a year ago.</p>
